.TH MVM 1 "2026-11-25" "mvm 0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mvm \- run dev tooling in throwaway Podman+krun microVMs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mvm fetch
.RB [ go | rust | node ]
.RB [ \-\-learn ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR CMD ...]
.br
.B mvm build
.RB [ go | rust | node ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-it ]
.B \-\-
.IR CMD ...
.br
.B mvm run \-i
.I IMAGE
.RB [ \-w
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-it ]
.B \-\-
.IR CMD ...
.br
.B mvm status
.br
.B mvm update
.br
.B mvm cache
.BR rm " NAME | " grow " NAME SIZE | " gc
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mvm
runs package managers, compilers and tests inside a hardware-virtualized
microVM
.RB ( podman (1)
with
.BR "\-\-runtime krun" ),
with no host privileges.
.PP
.B fetch
is the only command with network. It mounts a throwaway copy of the
dependency manifests only (go.mod, go.sum, go.work, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock,
package.json, package\-lock.json; Cargo target files as empty stubs), never the
sources. Without
.I CMD
it runs
.BR "go mod download" ,
.BR "cargo fetch" " (\-\-locked when Cargo.lock exists)" " or"
.BR "npm ci \-\-ignore\-scripts \-\-no\-audit \-\-no\-fund"
for every ecosystem found in the current directory. With
.I CMD
it runs that command instead, to change dependencies
.RB ( "go get" ", " "cargo add" ", " "npm install" ).
Manifests that changed are copied back into the project and listed.
.PP
The fetch VM has no direct network. Its only way out is TCP to one
host\-loopback port, where a per\-run Smokescreen proxy allows only the
ecosystem's registries (plus
.B [allow]
from the config); DNS, other TCP, UDP, ICMP and IPv6 are closed. Each
connection and denial is logged in the run record and summarised.
.B \-\-learn
lets every host through but logs it, commits nothing, and prints the hosts
outside the allowlist. Without the proxy binary
.RI ( ~/.local/lib/mvm/smokescreen ", built by " "make smokescreen" ),
fetch refuses to run.
.PP
.B build
runs offline in the current project, mounted read\-only at
.IR /src ,
with the ecosystem's caches: dependency caches read\-only, build caches and the
project's node_modules writable. The ecosystem is detected from the current
directory unless named.
.B run
does the same for any image, without caches.
.PP
In build and run, files and directories matching the mask list (default:
.IR ".git .env .env.* .envrc .npmrc .netrc .pypirc *.pem *.key id_rsa* id_ecdsa* id_ed25519*" )
are hidden: directories appear empty, files appear empty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-w " DIR"
Make
.I ./DIR
writable (created if missing; must be inside the project). Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-it
Interactive terminal.
.TP
.BI \-i " IMAGE"
Image for
.BR run .
.SH CACHES AND COMMIT-ON-CLEAN
Caches are sparse ext4 image files in
.IR ~/.cache/mvm ,
loop\-mounted inside the guest:
go\-mod, go\-build, cargo\-reg, cargo\-git, cargo\-target, npm, and one
nm\-<project>\-<hash> per node project.
A writable cache is reflink\-copied for the run and replaces the cache
atomically only when the command exits 0. Failure, interruption or a crash
leaves the cache unchanged. Each commit increments the cache's generation.
Readers take a shared
.BR flock (2),
the writer an exclusive one.
.TP
.B mvm cache gc
Remove leftover run copies, kill microVMs whose mvm process died, drop
node_modules caches of deleted projects.
.TP
.BI "mvm cache grow " "NAME SIZE"
Grow a cache image (refused while in use).
.TP
.BI "mvm cache rm " NAME
Delete a cache image (refused while in use).
.SH IMAGES
The first use of an image tag pins it to its digest in
.IR ~/.local/state/mvm/pins.json ;
later runs use the digest.
.B mvm update
re\-pulls every pinned tag and reports changes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mvm/config.toml
Optional:
.B mask
(list),
.B [images]
(go, rust, node),
.B [allow]
(go, rust, node: lists of extra hosts for fetch),
.B [memory]
(go, rust, node, run).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mvm/runs/
One JSON record per run (last 200).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR MVM_CACHE_DIR ", " MVM_STATE_DIR ", " MVM_CONFIG
override the paths above.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command's exit status; 2 for usage errors; 130 when interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mvm fetch
mvm fetch go \-\- go get golang.org/x/net@latest
mvm fetch rust \-\- cargo generate\-lockfile
mvm build \-w build \-\- go build \-o build/app ./cmd/app
mvm build node \-\- npm rebuild
mvm run \-i docker.io/library/alpine:3.24 \-\- uname \-a
.fi
.SH CAVEATS
podman's
.B \-\-tmpfs
is ignored under krun.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR podman\-run (1),
.BR flock (2)
